nchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A meta marshaller wraps the "},{"code":"closure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s marshal and modifies the way","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is called in some fashion. The most common use of this facility"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is for C callbacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same marshallers (generated by "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"#glib-genmarshal","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are used everywhere, but the way that we get the callback function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"differs. In most cases we want to use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"closure"},{"type":"text","text":"’s callback, but in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other cases we want to use some different technique to retrieve the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"callback function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, class closures for signals (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_signal_type_cclosure_new()"},{"text":") retrieve the callback function from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fixed offset in the class structure.  The meta marshaller retrieves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right callback and passes it to the marshaller as the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"marshalData"},{"type":"text","text":" argument."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glibobject\/closure\/setmetamarshal(marshaldata:metamarshal:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Closure","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/docu